<BaseLayout title={`About — ${AUTHOR_NAME}`} description="Benedikt Weishaupt — Product Designer.">
  <div class="bg-white text-gray-900">
    <article class="max-w-screen-md pt-8 pb-20 px-page">
      <div class="text-xl pb-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div>
          <p>Benedikt Weishaupt</p>
          <p class="text-gray-400">Product Designer</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <a href="mailto:mail@benediktweishaupt.de" class="underline underline-offset-4 decoration-gray-400 hover:decoration-gray-900 transition-colors">mail@benediktweishaupt.de</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <AboutTextSection>
        <p>Benedikt is a product designer. His projects move between early computational experiments and current tooling that lets design and development teams work towards a shared source of truth.</p>
        <p>Most recently, he's been working with reteach, an education technology company, to future-proof their LMS solution for SMEs. Over the past year, he architected and built their design system and the infrastructure that bridges design decisions to running code.</p>
        <p>Before that, he established product design at Closed in Hamburg, forming a cross-functional team to build their first design system following the rebrand—planning and implementing token pipelines that automate synchronization.</p>
        <p>Benedikt has taught and lectured across European institutions on algorithmic design practices—encouraging designers to treat code as material to build systems and workflows that work for their communities.</p>
      </AboutTextSection>

      <AboutItemList title="Selected Exhibitions & Lectures" items={exhibitions} />

      <AboutItemList title="Selected Teaching & Workshops" items={teaching} />

      <AboutTextSection>
        <p>Selected Clients</p>
        <p>reteach, Closed, Museum Utopie und Alltag, Mister Spex, SunExpress, wirDesign, KABK (Royal Academy of Art, The Hague), Sandberg Institute Amsterdam, Schwules Museum Berlin, Metahaven, Renzo Martens, Oettinger Publishing House, Here to Support, We Are Here, Elke Uitentuis</p>
      </AboutTextSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
